\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 1. App / Studio Split\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 Current state\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The existing App / Studio split is a good architectural decision.\
The native application build uses:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 npm run build:app\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 and Studio-only files are pruned before Capacitor copies the web bundle into the native projects.\
This means significant internal systems are already excluded from the IPA/APK, including areas such as:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
course mapping diagnostics;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
developer panels;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
course database administration;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
visual-engine authoring;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
course-play debug UI;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
conditions debug tooling;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
various Studio-only tuning surfaces.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The visual engine is also split so that the phone receives a much smaller play client rather than the complete authoring engine.\
This should be preserved.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Remaining problem\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The Netlify deployment works differently.\
Studio and the player web application share the same deployment and origin.\
Studio loads scripts from the same public:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 /scripts/*\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 directory.\
Consequently, a Studio-only JavaScript file can be absent from the player application\'92s HTML while still being directly retrievable from the public production CDN.\
Conceptually:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 Native build\
    \uc0\u8595 \
Studio code physically removed\
    \uc0\u8595 \
Good production boundary\
\
\
Netlify web deployment\
    \uc0\u8595 \
Player does not load Studio code\
    \uc0\u8595 \
Studio code still exists publicly on CDN\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 This means:\

\f0\b \'93Not loaded by the player UI\'94 is not currently equivalent to \'93not publicly delivered.\'94
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Recommendation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Eventually establish a genuine deployment/access boundary for Studio.\
Possible final architecture:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 Player production\
caddy.claritygolf.app\
        \uc0\u8595 \
Only player assets\
\
\
Internal Studio\
studio/internal deployment\
        \uc0\u8595 \
Authenticated/internal assets\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 The important improvement is the delivery boundary itself, not renaming the Studio JavaScript files.\
\
\uc0\u11835 \
