\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 12. Client Error Intake\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 /api/client-errors
\f1\fs24  is deliberately unauthenticated because it is designed to capture failures that may occur before authentication.\
That rationale is reasonable.\
It already has several useful protections:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 maximum 20 events/request\
64 KB request body\
message length limits\
detail length limits\
fingerprint deduplication\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 However, it accepts caller-provided:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 accountId\
message\
detail\
route\
source\
level\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 and writes them through a server-side service-role connection.\
The primary risk is not exposing the service-role key.\
The risk is:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
diagnostic spam;\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
misleading account IDs;\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
sensitive information accidentally entering 
\f2\fs26 detail
\f1\fs24 ;\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
tokens/URLs being captured;\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
unnecessary long-term retention of client diagnostics.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Recommendation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Eventually add:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 request/IP rate limiting\
strict field allowlist\
token/JWT redaction\
PII redaction\
server-derived account ID when authenticated\
diagnostic retention policy\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 This endpoint can remain unauthenticated if pre-login reporting remains important.\
\
\uc0\u11835 \
