\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 13. Admin Auth Door\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs26 \cf0 admin-auth-door
\f1\fs24  is protected by an environment token.\
That is good.\
It currently accepts the administrative token either through:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 Authorization: Bearer ...\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 or in the request body:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 adminToken\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 Recommendation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Eventually use the Authorization header exclusively.\
The endpoint also creates a temporary password using time plus 
\f2\fs26 Math.random()
\f1\fs24  before generating a recovery link.\
Since the administrator ultimately wants the password-setup/recovery link, investigate whether a usable temporary password is necessary at all.\
If a temporary credential genuinely is required, generate it using cryptographically secure randomness.\
This is not a primary production-delivery issue, but it is worth cleaning up.\
\
\uc0\u11835 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

